  "term": "bombesin",
  "definition": "Bombesin is a 14-amino-acid peptide first identified in the skin of certain toads and also found naturally in many animals, including mammals, where it acts as a neurotransmitter. It influences smooth muscle activity as well as stomach secretion and kidney blood flow and function.",
